1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,611
SOULHABIT: This bottle says eleven percent. Does
that mean eleven percent ectoin?

2
00:00:03,951 --> 00:00:06,283
SOULHABIT: No. It's a blend.

3
00:00:06,623 --> 00:00:09,949
SOULHABIT: Ectoin itself may genuinely help dry

4
00:00:09,969 --> 00:00:13,314
or stressed skin feel more comfortable.

5
00:00:13,594 --> 00:00:16,053
SOULHABIT: But the evidence is
limited, and it is

6
00:00:16,073 --> 00:00:18,552
not a miracle or
a replacement for treatment.

7
00:00:18,852 --> 00:00:22,214
SOULHABIT: Before skincare marketing found
it, ectoin belonged

8
00:00:22,234 --> 00:00:25,616
to a bacterium in
extremely salty water.

9
00:00:25,896 --> 00:00:28,894
JAY: Bacteria invented skincare?

10
00:00:29,174 --> 00:00:31,389
SOULHABIT: Not intentionally.

11
00:00:31,729 --> 00:00:35,576
SOULHABIT: The salt pulls water out
of the cell, turning it

12
00:00:35,596 --> 00:00:39,464
into a microscopic raisin. Ectoin
helps keep the machinery stable.

13
00:00:39,804 --> 00:00:44,203
SOULHABIT: Skincare borrowed the molecule.
Marketing borrowed the drama.

14
00:00:44,503 --> 00:00:47,491
SOULHABIT: Ectoin belongs to a group of

15
00:00:47,511 --> 00:00:50,519
protective molecules sometimes called extremolytes.

16
00:00:50,859 --> 00:00:54,221
SOULHABIT: Its effects involve how
water arranges around

17
00:00:54,241 --> 00:00:57,603
proteins. Scientists call part
of it preferential

18
00:00:57,623 --> 00:01:01,005
exclusion, though the real
picture is messier.

19
00:01:01,285 --> 00:01:05,490
JAY: Even the alarm wants
you to stop.

20
00:01:05,830 --> 00:01:09,998
SOULHABIT: Picture a protein as a
celebrity with security. Ectoin may

21
00:01:10,018 --> 00:01:14,206
help that water stay organised
without touching the protein directly.

22
00:01:14,546 --> 00:01:17,118
JAY: So ectoin gives

23
00:01:17,138 --> 00:01:19,730
proteins personal space.

24
00:01:20,030 --> 00:01:23,749
SOULHABIT: Laboratory research suggests ectoin may
help stabilise structures and change

25
00:01:23,769 --> 00:01:27,508
how keratin in the outer
skin layer interacts with water.

26
00:01:27,848 --> 00:01:31,109
SOULHABIT: It may help dry or
stressed skin cope more comfortably.

27
00:01:31,449 --> 00:01:34,773
JAY: Does ectoin create an invisible protective

28
00:01:34,793 --> 00:01:38,137
force field around my face?

29
00:01:38,417 --> 00:01:40,455
SOULHABIT: No. Not at all.

30
00:01:40,735 --> 00:01:43,501
JAY: Finally, a skincare ingredient

31
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:46,306
with realistic boundaries.

32
00:01:46,646 --> 00:01:50,623
SOULHABIT: Think of ectoin as support for
the skin barrier, not body armour.

33
00:01:50,923 --> 00:01:54,517
SOULHABIT: In one study, 104 women
compared a cream containing

34
00:01:54,537 --> 00:01:58,150
2 percent ectoin with the
same cream without it.

35
00:01:58,430 --> 00:02:00,818
SOULHABIT: The women preferred the ectoin version.

36
00:02:01,118 --> 00:02:03,712
JAY: So it worked?

37
00:02:03,992 --> 00:02:06,854
SOULHABIT: They liked it better. That
is real, but not

38
00:02:06,874 --> 00:02:09,755
the same as a machine
proving their skin changed.

39
00:02:10,056 --> 00:02:14,612
SOULHABIT: Another study followed 65 people with
mild to moderate eczema. Over four

40
00:02:14,632 --> 00:02:19,207
weeks the ectoin cream matched the
comparison and was well tolerated.

41
00:02:19,507 --> 00:02:20,982
JAY: Promising?

42
00:02:21,262 --> 00:02:22,362
SOULHABIT: Yes.

43
00:02:22,382 --> 00:02:23,804
JAY: Miracle?

44
00:02:24,084 --> 00:02:25,184
SOULHABIT: No.

45
00:02:25,204 --> 00:02:29,148
SOULHABIT: It does not prove ectoin cures
eczema or replaces treatment. The evidence

46
00:02:29,168 --> 00:02:33,131
is limited, and some research comes
from companies that sell it.

47
00:02:33,431 --> 00:02:36,584
SOULHABIT: A PubMed search found
twelve clinical trials.

48
00:02:36,864 --> 00:02:39,927
JAY: Twelve? My group chat
has produced more research

49
00:02:39,947 --> 00:02:43,029
on whether someone should
text their ex.

50
00:02:43,329 --> 00:02:47,332
SOULHABIT: Ectoin suits dry, sensitive
or irritated skin, and

51
00:02:47,352 --> 00:02:51,374
pairs with panthenol, glycerin,
squalane and ceramides.

52
00:02:51,714 --> 00:02:54,778
SOULHABIT: Exactly. Check the actual percentage
when it is disclosed,

53
00:02:54,798 --> 00:02:57,883
read the ingredient list and
judge the complete formula.

54
00:02:58,163 --> 00:03:01,096
JAY: One fashionable ingredient cannot rescue

55
00:03:01,116 --> 00:03:04,069
a badly built product.

56
00:03:04,349 --> 00:03:06,969
SOULHABIT: You may deactivate the
Jargon Alarm now.

57
00:03:07,269 --> 00:03:11,781
SOULHABIT: K-beauty did not invent ectoin.
Bacteria developed the survival strategy.

58
00:03:11,802 --> 00:03:16,334
Korean formulators pair it with
barrier ingredients in light textures.

59
00:03:16,614 --> 00:03:19,559
JAY: So bacteria invented it, and

60
00:03:19,579 --> 00:03:22,544
Korea gave it better packaging.

61
00:03:22,844 --> 00:03:26,133
SOULHABIT: Ectoin is not the new
hyaluronic acid, not a

62
00:03:26,153 --> 00:03:29,462
miracle, and the evidence does
not support dramatic promises.

63
00:03:29,762 --> 00:03:33,556
SOULHABIT: It is a genuinely
interesting supporting ingredient

64
00:03:33,577 --> 00:03:37,391
that may help dry
or stressed skin.

65
00:03:37,671 --> 00:03:41,126
JAY: Supporting actor, not superhero.

66
00:03:41,426 --> 00:03:45,933
SOULHABIT: Exactly. Look for the actual percentage,
then judge the whole formula.

67
00:03:46,233 --> 00:03:49,721
JAY: And would I put
a bacteria-made survival molecule

68
00:03:49,741 --> 00:03:53,229
on my face? I
already bought snail mucus.

69
00:03:53,249 --> 00:03:56,757
The dignity ship sailed years ago.

70
00:03:57,057 --> 00:04:01,062
JAY: What questionable skincare ingredient
are we investigating next?
